ORION-EA quantum handoff after #957/#963 closure: QG-20 is a much better exact quantum crossover than a generic 'LLM + quantum' benchmark.

If QG-20 exposes a frozen mixed-cell / exact-quotient residual, a learned proposer can be tested **proposal-side only**: given permitted training-side counterexamples/state traces, propose a new executable human-readable coordinate intended to refine the current compiler-state vocabulary. QG-20 remains the scientific owner/referee and decides whether the coordinate actually separates quotient classes / transfers to held-out continuations.

Mandatory controls from EA research:
- generic feature synthesis / partition refinement / program synthesis get the same evidence and budget;
- if exact quotient refinement directly constructs the needed coordinate, credit the exact method, not the LLM;
- no finite hidden feature menu if exhaustive verification fits the budget (`EAJ_FINITE_MENU_CLASS_CLOSED`);
- candidate coordinate must be frozen before protected continuation outcomes;
- identity/remint changes are not semantic-coordinate discoveries;
- quantum theorem/quotient ownership stays QG-20.

This is a possible P10/P11/Jump consumer of QG-20, not a new quantum claim under EA.
